Let \(K\subseteq\mathbb{R}^n\) be a full-dimensional closed convex cone, let \(\varepsilon\ge0\), and set \(\tau(x):=\varepsilon\max\{1,\|x\|_2\}\). A scale-aware test may declare \(x\) approximately feasible when \(d_K(x)\le\tau(x)\), robustly interior when \(d_{
\mathbb{R}^n\setminus K}(x)>\tau(x)\), and near-boundary when both \(d_K(x)\le\tau(x)\) and \(d_{
\mathbb{R}^n\setminus K}(x)\le\tau(x)\). Points satisfying none of these predicates remain numerically unclassified.
